document.write(' Serena Williams may be planning a return to the tour by April, having told Fed Cup captain Mary Joe Fernandez she will be available to play for the U.S. in the semifinals of the team competition.\"Earlier this morning Serena emailed me. She\'s going to make herself available for the April tie,\" said Fernandez on ESPN, citing next summer\'s Olympics as Williams\' motivation to play.Players must make themselves available for Fed Cup duty twice before each Olympics to be eligible for the Games. The U.S.A will have to defeat Belgium in next month\'s quarterfinals for Williams\' services to be needed.Williams has been sidelined since just after Wimbledon, undergoing two surgeries for a toe injury sustained by stepping on glass at a resturant. She has not set a date for her return.\"So it\'s a good sign for me that she\'s thinking ahead to the Olympics,\" said Fernandez. \"She\'s still in the boot, hoping to get out of it by February.\"');
