document.write('DURHAM, N.C. (AP)?Leading junior tennis player Beatrice Capra has signed a letter of intent to go to Duke. The 18-year-old Capra, of Ellicott City, Md., earned attention at last year?s U.S. Open by reaching the third round. Making her Grand Slam debut while ranked 371st, Capra upset 18th-seeded Aravane Rezai and 95th-ranked Karolina Sprem in New York, before losing to three-time major champion Maria Sharapova. Duke and the U.S. Tennis Association both announced Capra?s signing. Patrick McEnroe, general manager of USTA player development, said in a statement released Wednesday that the USTA supports Capra?s decision and feels ?strongly that collegiate tennis can be part of one?s pathway to pro tennis.?');
